\f1\b\fs36 \cf2 Performance Optimization of a Flyback Converter for Isolated Power Supply
\f0\b0\fs32 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 1. Topic:
\f0\b0  Stability and Performance Analysis, Controller Tuning\

\f1\b 2. Problem: 
\f0\b0 A flyback converter is designed for an isolated 5V output from a 100V DC input. The converter must maintain regulation under load variations from 0.5A to 2A.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 3. Tasks:
\f0\b0 \
- Model the flyback converter and derive the small-signal transfer function for control design.\
- Tune the PI controller parameters (Kp, Ki) to achieve fast transient response with minimal overshoot and output ripple.\
- Define an optimization criterion (e.g., minimize settling time with less than 2% overshoot) and select the best controller parameters accordingly, justifying the choice for industrial reliability.\

\f1\b 4. Importance:
\f0\b0 \
- Critical for reliable power delivery in industrial applications\
- Ensures stable operation under dynamic load conditions\
- Prevents system failures in sensitive electronic equipment\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 5. Market Relevance:
\f0\b0 \
- Essential for power supplies in industrial automation, telecom, and medical devices\
- Meets growing demand for efficient, compact isolated power solutions\
- Addresses industry needs for robust power management in harsh environments\
